            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A GaAs substrate that is a group III-V compound semiconductor substrate includes particles of greater than or equal to 0.079 µm in particle size at less than or equal to 0.6 particles/cm&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;2&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; on the main surface. An epilayer-attached GaAs substrate that is an epilayer-attached group III-V compound semiconductor substrate includes the GaAs substrate mentioned above and an epitaxial layer disposed on the main surface of the GaAs substrate, and includes LPDs of greater than or equal to 3.0 µm in circle-equivalent diameter at less than or equal to 5 defects/cm&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;2&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; on the main surface in a case where the epitaxial layer has a thickness of 5 µm. Thus, a group III-V compound semiconductor substrate and an epilayer-attached group III-V compound semiconductor substrate are provided which can reduce defects of the epitaxial layer grown on the main surface.</p>
            </abstract>
